<title>UK: NWE naphtha weakens with crude, but still quiet.</title>
<headline>NWE naphtha weakens with crude, but still quiet.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE naphtha was weaker in line with sharp drops in crude futures.</p>
<p>Traders said activity was slow with several major players still out of the market.</p>
<p>Naphtha was pegged around $215-216 cif NWE for prompt material, down $1-2 from Wednesday's levels. Swaps were similarily weaker.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a difficult market, there really is not enough happening,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
